# Session hygiene

Every turn carries the whole chat with it, so a chat that outlives its slice
costs more each turn and remembers less accurately. Watch for the boundary and
name it — once.

## Say it when

- The slice is finished: G4 passed, docs updated, work committed
- The conversation has been summarized or compacted (context is already being dropped)
- The next request belongs to a different Spec than the one this chat has built
- The chat has carried two or more Specs end to end

## Do not

- Repeat the suggestion turn after turn, or after the Orchestrator has declined it
- Stop work or ask them to restart before answering what they just asked — finish the turn first
- Raise it mid-slice, while a Spec is half-built or a bug is half-diagnosed

## How to say it

One line at the end of the reply, in the language of the conversation, carrying
the handoff the next chat needs:

> Slice 0036 khép lại ở đây. Chat mới nên bắt đầu bằng: "Đọc
> `docs/specs/0037` và 15 dòng cuối `DECISIONS-LOG.md`, rồi build slice C1."

The pointer matters more than the suggestion. A fresh chat is only cheaper if
it starts from the documents instead of re-deriving the context by reading the
codebase — which is exactly what `docs/specs`, `CONTEXT.md` and the decisions
log exist for.
